{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"c0e600c4332f7377","name":"card_event_lysander_pl","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Poland/units/card_event_lysander_pl","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"LYSANDER PL","text":"When the enemy plays a known card, deal 1 damage to the enemy HQ.","flavorText":"The Westland Lysander was a British made cooperation and liaison aircraft that came into service in 1938 and was used by RAF and Allied air forces during WWII. The aircraft was mainly used for artillery spotting or message and supply drops, but was withdrawn from combat duties after the Battle of France due to high losses inflicted by German fighters. For the remainder of the war the Lysander served mainly in liaison and air-sea rescue roles. The aircraft was used to maintain contact with the French Resistance, for supply drops, delivering and retrieving agents or to rescue downed pilots that were sheltered in France. Several Lysander aircraft were used by the No. 309 Polish Fighter-Reconnaissance Squadron, but from 1942 the squadron started to transition to Mustangs. A total 1,786 Westland Lysander’s were built, including a few variants. ","faction":"Poland","type":"fighter","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":2,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":2},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_lysander_pl","title":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_lysander_pl_title","SourceString":"LYSANDER PL","LocalizedString":"LYSANDER PL"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":1,"defense":2,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Poland","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_lysander_pl_text","SourceString":"When the enemy plays a known card, deal 1 damage to the enemy HQ.","LocalizedString":"When the enemy plays a known card, deal 1 damage to the enemy HQ."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_lysander_pl_history","SourceString":"The Westland Lysander was a British made cooperation and liaison aircraft that came into service in 1938 and was used by RAF and Allied air forces during WWII. The aircraft was mainly used for artillery spotting or message and supply drops, but was withdrawn from combat duties after the Battle of France due to high losses inflicted by German fighters. For the remainder of the war the Lysander served mainly in liaison and air-sea rescue roles. The aircraft was used to maintain contact with the French Resistance, for supply drops, delivering and retrieving agents or to rescue downed pilots that were sheltered in France. Several Lysander aircraft were used by the No. 309 Polish Fighter-Reconnaissance Squadron, but from 1942 the squadron started to transition to Mustangs. A total 1,786 Westland Lysander’s were built, including a few variants. ","LocalizedString":"The Westland Lysander was a British made cooperation and liaison aircraft that came into service in 1938 and was used by RAF and Allied air forces during WWII. The aircraft was mainly used for artillery spotting or message and supply drops, but was withdrawn from combat duties after the Battle of France due to high losses inflicted by German fighters. For the remainder of the war the Lysander served mainly in liaison and air-sea rescue roles. The aircraft was used to maintain contact with the French Resistance, for supply drops, delivering and retrieving agents or to rescue downed pilots that were sheltered in France. Several Lysander aircraft were used by the No. 309 Polish Fighter-Reconnaissance Squadron, but from 1942 the squadron started to transition to Mustangs. A total 1,786 Westland Lysander’s were built, including a few variants. "},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WorldAtWar","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnCounterMeasureTriggered"],"cipher":2,"exileNation":"EFactionEnum::Britain","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectNam